      "text": "### Survey — Finding Sites Before You Dig"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#007",
      "path": [
        "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:anthropology:06-archaeology, git-history:anthropology:06-archaeology]",
        "canonical_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "current_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:anthropology:archaeology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "anthropology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "section": "anthropology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  PEDESTRIAN SURVEY:\n  Systematic coverage of a study area on foot, at regular\n  intervals. Crew members walk parallel transects, record\n  surface artifacts, features, and site boundaries."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#008",
      "path": [
        "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:anthropology:06-archaeology, git-history:anthropology:06-archaeology]",
        "canonical_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "current_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:anthropology:archaeology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "anthropology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "section": "anthropology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Sampling strategies:\n  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ FULL COVERAGE: survey entire study area. Most complete.│\n  │ Impractical for large areas.                           │\n  │                                                        │\n  │ RANDOM SAMPLING: randomly select transects/units.      │\n  │ Statistically defensible; misses spatially clustered   │\n  │ sites.                                                 │\n  │                                                        │\n  │ STRATIFIED SAMPLING: divide area into environmental    │\n  │ zones; sample each proportionally. Better for          │\n  │ heterogeneous landscapes.                              │\n  │                                                        │\n  │ JUDGMENTAL SAMPLING: survey where you think sites      │\n  │ are (near water, on ridges). Efficient but biased.     │\n  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#009",
      "path": [
        "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:anthropology:06-archaeology, git-history:anthropology:06-archaeology]",
        "canonical_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "current_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:anthropology:archaeology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "anthropology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "section": "anthropology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SITE DEFINITION: a spatial concentration of artifacts\n  and/or features above background noise. \"Background noise\"\n  is determined from offsite sampling.\n```"
    },
