      },
      "text": "### Excavation — The Irreversible Act"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#011",
      "path": [
        "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:anthropology:06-archaeology, git-history:anthropology:06-archaeology]",
        "canonical_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "current_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:anthropology:archaeology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "anthropology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "section": "anthropology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  KEY INSIGHT: excavation destroys the context it recovers.\n  You cannot re-excavate. Meticulous documentation is\n  not bureaucracy — it is the only way the data persists."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:anthropology:06-archaeology, git-history:anthropology:06-archaeology]",
        "canonical_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "current_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:anthropology:archaeology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "anthropology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "section": "anthropology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STRATIGRAPHIC METHOD:\n  Remove deposits layer by layer, following natural\n  stratigraphy (the actual depositional layers), not\n  arbitrary depth levels (which cut across strata and\n  mix contexts)."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:anthropology:06-archaeology, git-history:anthropology:06-archaeology]",
        "canonical_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "current_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:anthropology:archaeology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "anthropology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "section": "anthropology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHEELER BOX-GRID (Mortimer Wheeler, 1930s):\n  Grid of 10x10m (or similar) squares with baulks (unexcavated\n  walls) between them, preserving stratigraphy for reading.\n  The baulk lets you see the full stratigraphic sequence as\n  a visible cross-section. Dominant method through mid-20th c."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#014",
      "path": [
        "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:anthropology:06-archaeology, git-history:anthropology:06-archaeology]",
        "canonical_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "current_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:anthropology:archaeology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "anthropology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "section": "anthropology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "OPEN AREA EXCAVATION (single context recording):\n  Remove baulks; expose the full horizontal extent of each\n  depositional unit (context) before moving to the next.\n  Better for understanding spatial organization of features.\n  Now dominant in European urban/settlement archaeology."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#015",
      "path": [
        "06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:anthropology:06-archaeology, git-history:anthropology:06-archaeology]",
        "canonical_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "current_path": "anthropology/06-ARCHAEOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:anthropology:archaeology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "anthropology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[archaeology]",
        "section": "anthropology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RECORDING:\n  Each \"context\" (discrete deposit, layer, feature, cut)\n  gets its own context sheet: stratigraphic relationships,\n  soil description, finds, samples, spatial data.\n  Total station survey: sub-centimeter 3D coordinates on\n  artifacts in situ. Site drawings + photography + digital.\n```"
    }
